# Not committed: Cloudflare's Workers Build runs `npm ci` whenever a
# lockfile is present, which hit a version-compatibility failure between
# our local npm (10.9.7) and Cloudflare's build image (npm 10.9.2) even
# with a lockfile that's genuinely in sync with package.json. Nothing at
# deploy time needs it anyway — wrangler bundles TypeScript itself and
# fetches its own copy fresh via npx regardless of what's installed. Keep
# lockfiles local-only for reproducible dev/test installs.
package-lock.json
